      ":question/id": "2c8cf324-472b-5836-8692-8d44663200a5",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1101",
      ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{log}⁡\\left(\\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)+{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(ab)$ - the product rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)$ - the quotient rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡({c}^{m})=m{log}_{n}⁡(c)$ - the power rule\n\nUsing the quotient rule and then the power rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡\\left(\\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(3y)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
