      ":question/id": "a8ef19a1-f2fa-5f29-a4ae-a1f3f6bb227d",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1110",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-5{log}_{5}⁡(y)$ as a single logarithm.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)+{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(ab)$ - the product rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)$ - the quotient rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡({c}^{m})=m{log}_{n}⁡(c)$ - the power rule\n\nUsing the power rule and then the quotient rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-5{log}_{5}⁡(y) & ={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{1/2})-{log}_{5}⁡({y}^{5}) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(\\sqrt{x})-{log}_{5}⁡({y}^{5}) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{y}^{5}}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
